NRC7394 Software Package - Licensing Overview
=============================================

This repository contains components under several different licenses. There is
no single license that applies to the repository as a whole.

The license of each file is declared either in the file itself, as an
SPDX-License-Identifier tag, or in REUSE.toml for files that cannot contain a
comment (firmware images, board data, documents and prebuilt binaries).

Full license texts are in the LICENSES/ directory.
A component-by-component explanation is in LICENSING.md.


Component map
-------------

  Component                              License
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  package/src/nrc/                       ISC
  package/src/nrc_hspi_simple/           ISC
  package/src/cli_app/                   MIT
  package/src/ft232h-usb-spi/            GPL-2.0-only
                                           (c) DENX Software Engineering
  package/src/ch347-usb-spi/             GPL-2.0-or-later
                                           (c) Nanjing Qinheng Micro. (WCH)

  Firmware images and board data         LicenseRef-NewracomFirmware
    (*.bin, *.dat)

  Prebuilt binaries
    nrc.ko                               ISC      (built from package/src/nrc/)
    cli_app                              MIT      (built from package/src/cli_app/)

  Scripts, configuration and dts         ISC

  Documentation (*.pdf)                  LicenseRef-NewracomDoc

  Bundled Wireshark packages (*.deb)     GPL-2.0-or-later
    package/evk/sw_pkg/nrc_pkg/script/sniffer/
    Corresponding source is published with the release; see the README in
    that directory.


Verifying
---------

This project follows the REUSE Specification 3.3 (https://reuse.software).
Every file carries licensing information. To verify:

    pipx install reuse
    reuse lint


Previous releases
-----------------

Releases up to and including v1.3.2 were distributed with a single GPL-2.0
license file at the repository root. The per-file notices in those releases
were unchanged from v1.0 onward and are the same as the ones shown above. The
terms under which any previous release was received are not affected by this
document. See LICENSING.md for details.


